/E (This is a compiler-introduced security bug, or CISB. The code is simplified from our b_ptr02 control. At -O2, InstCombine removes the wrap half of the check. On a crafted length, the -O0 build stops at the guard, while the optimized build crashes inside memcpy. The compiler did nothing wrong by the C standard, which is what makes these bugs hard to find.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
